# Pago

Consumer client (`server/lib/pago.js`) against `https://pago.cloud`, OAuth `grant_type=pago`. App login is these credentials. The client writes them on the pago doc (`loginStatus: PENDING`) and the ticker logs in, stores the token payload (`access_token`, `refresh_token` if present), and deletes `password`. Later runs use the tokens.

The daily `pago` job reads `GET /pos_v1_1/provider/fetch/{accountUuid}` (`accountUuid` from `GET /authentication/uaa/v1.00/user_profile`). Each nested location is a consumption point. Its name is `locationLabel` or `service`. An invoice is unpaid when `amountDue` is set. A tenant matches a point when the names are equal, trimmed and case-insensitive. Those invoices are written onto the tenant as `invoices`. When `notifications` is true and the tenant has an email, unpaid PDFs (`GET /pos_v1_1/provider/pdfbytes/{invoiceId}`) are attached and mailed. `mailed[invoiceId]` is `"new"` the first time an invoice is seen before its due date, and `"overdue"` once the due date has passed. An invoice that is already overdue the first time it is seen gets only the overdue mail. `syncedAt` on the pago doc skips another pass the same day.

Also on `pago.cloud`:

- `POST /sdk/bills/accounts` — `activeAccounts` can be empty even with `hasConnectedAccounts: true`.
- `GET /sdk/bills/providers` — supplier catalog (`id`, `name`, `uri`, enrolment `status`). Not the user's connected accounts.
- `GET /payment/payment-details-v2?paymentEntityType=INVOICE` — first payment per `invoice.locationId`.
- `GET /payment/transactions` — `locationId` only, no street.
